title: gio: sys's windows, drawn in go
state: open

a poc of `sh/window` and of studio's top row, in gio (gioui.org). open: the
call to make is whether to switch to it.

    todo/gio/build          into ~/.cache/sys-gio/window
    todo/gio/build test     vet and tests; sys's ./build goes first
    PATH=~/.cache/sys-gio:$HOME/src/sys/bin:$PATH window -studio .
    ... fm -w               the same view, for one program

what is where
    main.go     the window: input and drawing, the one file that knows gio
    ft.go       text by freetype, sharp as the terminal's
    host.go     fm and ed -f, each at the other end of a pipe
    look.go     studio's look, made again from the nodes
    model.go    moving, open and close, made again: see the views entry

its own go module, so that sys takes on neither gio nor cgo.

keys: ctrl-w the other pane, a stand-in; ctrl-shift-v paste; f11.

careful: it edits real files, and closing the window drops what ed has
not saved. q in fm keeps it.

before it can replace a daily view
    - [ ] closing the window keeps unsaved work
    - [ ] a shell, in the window or beside it. untried idea: tmux runs it,
      capture-pane -e gives the screen, send-keys takes the input
    - [ ] help and the pickers: the term entry in todo/next
    - [ ] the wheel scrolls, and paste is seen to work
    - [ ] f11 is seen to work
also missing: thumbs, tree brackets, studio/frame, the lens.
